  The PET machine itself (bus, memories, CRTC, picture, keyboard, registers) in trx/ is written for this project and follows pet2001hw.v in what the
  hardware does; no line of it is copied.

Not vendored (no ROM bytes in this repository): the PET ROMs (BASIC, editor, KERNAL, character set) are the person's files, put through the
core application at run time (Commodore ROMs, clean room).

trx/pet_spet.v (the SuperPET board registers, Q13) is written for this project from the behaviour of VICE's pet/petmem.c (read as the reference, no code copied).

trx/pet_pixw.v, pet_win.v, pet_regs.v, pet_audio.v are derived from the C264 core's modules of the same author (cores/c264/rtl/trx, T90).

